    <string name="tutorial_goal_title">Welcome to Dipole</string>
    <string name="tutorial_goal">White and Black each start with one stack of 12 checkers. Only the dark squares are used, and White moves first. Take all of your opponent’s checkers out of play to win.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_moving_title">Moving</string>
    <string name="tutorial_moving">Tap one of your stacks to see where it can go. A stack moves exactly as many squares as the checkers you move, so this stack of 4 can go 1, 2, 3 or 4 squares. You can move part of a stack, and moves jump over anything in between.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_plain_title">Plain moves and merges</string>
    <string name="tutorial_plain">Moves to an empty square, or onto one of your own stacks to merge with it, go forward or diagonally forward only. Moving straight ahead needs an even number of checkers.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_captures_title">Captures</string>
    <string name="tutorial_captures">Land on an enemy stack no bigger than the checkers you move to capture all of it. Captures (red) go in any direction, even backwards. Here the stack of 3 is too big for 2 checkers.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_off_board_title">Moving off the board</string>
    <string name="tutorial_off_board">A plain move may go past the edge of the board. Those checkers leave play for good. Choose these moves with the buttons under the board.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_sitting_out_title">Sitting out</string>
    <string name="tutorial_sitting_out">Moving is mandatory. A player with no legal move sits out while the other keeps playing. Here Black’s checker can neither move forward nor capture, so Black sits out.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tips_title">Winning and tips</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tips">The game ends when one player has no checkers left. Stuck? Tap Hint, then one of your stacks, and its best move blinks on the board. Undo takes back your last move.</string>
